# Build artifacts
bin/
build/
tmp/

# Dependencies
vendor/

# Not used: Tailwind is a standalone binary irgo downloads, so there is no
# Node toolchain here. These only appear if something reintroduces one.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
bun.lock

# Generated files
*_templ.go
static/css/output.css

# go.work is created by `irgo app build/run android|ios` (gomobile needs it)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Native shells are generated by the irgo CLI (irgo app build/run ios|android
# self-scaffold) from its embedded templates — NOT checked in.
ios/Example/
# ios/App is the SwiftPM/xtool shell used for iOS on Linux.
ios/App/
android/Example/

# Android example build outputs + machine-local SDK path
android/Example/build/
android/Example/.gradle/
android/Example/app/build/
android/Example/app/libs/irgo.aar
android/Example/local.properties

# Store packages produced by `irgo app package`.
#
# irgo.package.toml is NOT ignored: it is shared config (app version, export
# method, store IDs) your team needs. Secrets go in irgo.package.local.toml,
# which is ignored, or in environment variables — which is how CI supplies them.
# appicon.png is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the single source icon YOU
# provide, and every platform icon is derived from it at build time. Ignoring
# it meant an icon never reached CI or teammates, so builds silently shipped
# the platform default.
dist/
irgo.package.local.toml

# Backups written by `irgo project upgrade` when it replaces a file that had changed.
# Safe to delete once you have checked you did not lose a local edit.
*.irgo-bak

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
build-errors.log

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# Refreshed from the Go module by `irgo project assets` on every build, when a
# project depends on the Morpheus component kit. Committing them would be a
# second copy of someone else's release that goes stale the moment the
# dependency moves — and the version cannot drift while they come from the
# module the wrappers were compiled against.
#
# Your own stylesheets, including your own themes, live in static/css beside
# this directory and are never touched.
static/css/morpheus/
static/js/morpheus.js

# .claude/settings.local.json is per-machine assistant settings — personal.
#
# .claude/skills is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike the other generated
# output above. Every build refreshes it out of the Go modules you depend on,
# but an assistant reads it the moment the repository is cloned, which is
# before any build has run. Ignoring it meant the reference that stops
# `data-attr-class` being written instead of `data-attr:class` was absent
# exactly when it was needed.
.claude/settings.local.json
